I am a big fan of Dishonored, and I am writing my first game review because I was quite sad after finishing this game.
I can't rate it low, the first half of the game was brilliant, I was enjoying every second, every decision. Been playing on the Very Hard difficulty to fully enjoy stealth nonlethal. And in the opposite to everything good in the first part of the game, second become boring, very linear, with tons of enemies, so you just have to rush to the victory, which is kind of not what you excpect from this game.
Total:
First 3 episodes = 10/10 "Beautiful, interesting contracts, crazy new powers";
4 episode = 5/10 "The episode where game pushes you to start rushing";
5 episode = 3/10 "Totaly linear map. You will waste a lot of time figuring out the path through the horde of cultists. May be it can be fun, not for me";
Ending = "Very short, sidequests didn't affect the ending".
Summarising:
I will recommend you to play this game if:
a) this is the last of the series Dishonored (if at the time you read this there is the next part of this series, just skip this one);
b) you are a big fan of Dishonored and stealth games like I am.
Thanks for reading my review of this game, hope it was helpful!

