I was cautiously optimistic about CIV:BE but after a few play throughs I’m left quite disappointed. While there are some good ideas here (the web tech tree, affinities, more customisations for races) most have been poorly executed or feel like they were never tested:
•	The UI has gone backwards since Civ 5;
•	Balance is pretty woeful atm (trade routes are the be all and end all; most wonders are a waste, some questionable unit strength values);
•	AI is so pathetic it might as well be a placeholder  (If combat wasn’t bad enough, the AI now has no idea how to navigate the complex tech tree or deal with the multiple terrain improvement options);
•	Some basic game customising options are missing;
•	Generally bland & uninspiring (nations have no unique building/units, and bonuses for the most part so are insignificant that there’s almost no difference between them);
•	The Aliens, while a great idea end up being little more than barbarians (but had so much potential); and
•	Some game features are so tedious (trade routes and specialists, I’m looking at you!).
Now just to be clear I’m not suggesting never get this game, but I’d strongly suggested that you wait for it to go on sale and see what the modding community can do down the track to fix up this mess.

