I like this metroidvania:
- the combat feels substantial and the boss battles are tough but not too tough;
- the graphic design is lovely, a great mix of cute and grotesque;
- the levels intertwine and feel like they are alive with character, they're interesting to explore with lots of secrets to find;
- and there are some lovely touches along the way that show a lot of care and attention, like how you can find the mapmaker in each level by following his paper trail, or how you can hear that there are secret grubs somewhere close by so you can put extra effort into exploring every nook and cranny.
Very good.

