It's impossible not to make the comparison with Darkest Dungeon, which seems to have directly inspired a great amount of mechanics in 'The Storm Guard';
So, for the purpose of the review;
Have you played Darkest Dungeon? No? Get that instead, it's the better game.
Yes? Great, this will scratch much the same itch, but wil tread more familiar ground while doing it; Grid-based combat where yo move units around, status changes and counters - all the usual.
A more than adequate game for the price, about 15-20 hours to see all content - solid 7/10 average title.

The game looks like a classic blocky fps, very funny and the weapons are balanced. The characters are a bit slow but overall okay.There are a map and characters editors.Matches are full of strange players, from the default skin to user created characters like comics characters or games one, I personally made a Finn skin from "adventure Time".
PRO:
-Fully destructible maps, and rebuildable with cubes supplied to players;
-balanced weapons (there are not many);
-map editor and characters, easy to use and fun to see the results;
BAD:
-few actual players (many empty server, the ones with someone inside are never more than 5-6)
-sniper rifle is too difficult to use but instakill
-the user created characters become public and can be used by everyone, it would be nice to let the creator decide if make them public or private for personal use only.
Overall a good game and very very fun. The bade aren't that bad, sadly few person play it! Spread the game guys!!

PROS:
- Fun experience of hacking and slashing;
- Funny dialogs between the characters AND Lo-Wang talking to himself;
- Gorgeous lighting filters and dinamic shadows;
- New skill features, you can upgrade your character and acquire some habilities;
- It's like a "how Lo-Wang became the♥♥♥♥♥kicking warrior from the first game";
- You can perform a dash. KEEP DASHING, BRO. JUST DO IT.
- It's gory. C'mon, it's fun.
CONS:
- Nice background story, but a half♥♥♥♥♥story for the playthrough;
- It's linear. Don't expect an open world experience (it's not that bad, but it's good to keep it in mind).
- Pretty below average graphics for a 2013 game (it's like a 2008 game, like The Witcher, with 2013 shaders);
- Gun based combat is pretty weird. The game kinda forces you to use Shurikens and Swords in order to perform some really effective attacks.
I'd say it's a fun experience, but full of repetitive fights over and over. The game is fast paced and gives you some challenge if you play in the higher difficulties (good thing for those who like action games). But if you're not used to melee first person combat  focused game, you're going to get your♥♥♥♥♥kicked.
Anyway, It's not cool denying the merit of the game. It has it's milestones and has the potential to provide you with a nice amount of fun hours.
If you think the price is good, just buy it and slash some demons.
